# CLUSTER run (2026-11-08; user: "if the local run looks good - start on cluster"): the
# local plain-SAC fine-tune of c0 (slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac_plain.env) on the cluster's
# two towns, Town05 and Town01 at once (user 2026-10-21), with in-job evals
# (slurm/train_with_evals.sbatch).
#   * From c0 (il_bc_c0/step_15000), encoder + GRU frozen; c0's demos preloaded and
#     PINNED with the arrival approach cut, never moving the temperature; critic warm-up
#     5000 updates, then the actor frozen for the first 5000 online updates (run S2's
#     recipe, slurm/sac_c0_trunk_a02_demos.env).
#   * Rewards x10 IN THE ENVIRONMENT (REWARD_SCALE; HER's relabelled rows and the demos
#     get the same x10 where they enter the replay).
#   * PLAIN SAC (user rule 2026-11-08, slurm/plain_sac.env, sourced last): no value clips,
#     actor loss alpha*logpi - Q, learned log-std, auto-tuned temperature, no pre-tanh
#     penalty, no PER, every transition equally likely, no forced goal/explore split.
#   * Demos of the TRAINING towns only, as in the local run (which preloads Town05's
#     for Town05): IL_PRELOAD_TOWNS="Town05 Town01". S2 took the default, all four
#     recorded towns (Town01/04/05/10HD, 380k pinned rows), so at the actor's release
#     most of its batches were demos of towns it never drove.
# Differs from the local run only in: two towns (one CARLA 0.9.16 server each, in the
# container) instead of Town05 on the host's 0.9.15, so one update per 5 steps is 32
# replayed samples per new transition (local: 64); demos of both training towns.
. "$REPO/slurm/sac_c0_trunk_a02_demos.env"
export REWARD_SCALE=10 IL_PRELOAD_TOWNS="Town05 Town01"
. "$REPO/slurm/plain_sac.env"
